.TH INZONE-SERVICE 1 "2026-10-04" "inzone-linux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inzone-service \- provide INZONE controls over the session D-Bus
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inzone-service
.RB [ --offline ]
.br
.B inzone-service --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B inzone-service
serves the INZONE desktop interface through the desktop user's session D-Bus.
D-Bus activation or the
.B inzone-control.service
user unit normally starts it when needed.
.PP
The well-known bus name is
.BR dev.zeroday0619 ,
the object path is
.BR /dev/zeroday0619 ,
and the control interface is
.BR dev.zeroday0619.Control1 .
Requests use the same profile and device controllers as the command-line
interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.B --offline
Disable hardware and audio operations for isolated diagnostics.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/services/dev.zeroday0619.service
Session D-Bus activation configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/inzone-control.service
Systemd user service unit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR inzone-gui (1),
.BR inzone-profile (1),
.BR dbus-daemon (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
